<%#
  "Optional", beside a label, in the console's accent rather than in grey.

  Grey is the colour this console uses for prose you may skip, and that is the
  opposite of what this word is for: it is the one thing on a card of identical
  boxes that tells a developer they can stop. It gets read or the card costs
  them ten minutes hunting for a value their account does not have.

  purple-900 on white is 15.09:1 and purple-300 on the dark card 6.64:1 -- both
  well past the 4.5:1 this size of text needs, which is worth stating because
  an accent colour used for small text is the usual place that floor is missed.
%>
<span class="ml-2 text-xs font-medium text-purple-900 dark:text-purple-300">Optional</span>
